' 4+1 process view - Deactivate an owner (US29) · conditional update, audit record and revocation in one transaction
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: Conditional update, audit record and session revocation in a single transaction (US29).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-owner-deactivation
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - deactivate an owner (US29): conditional update, audit record and revocation in one transaction
autonumber

participant "Owner page" as WEB_F_ADMIN
box "ASP.NET Core API"
  participant "Authorization" as CC_AUTHZ
  participant "Administration" as API_ADMIN
end box
database "users" as DB_USERS
database "owner_status_changes" as DB_STATUSCHG
database "refresh_tokens" as DB_REFRESH

WEB_F_ADMIN -> CC_AUTHZ : POST /api/admin/owners/{id}/deactivate { reason } [apiJson]
CC_AUTHZ -> API_ADMIN : Admin session (otherwise 401 or 403) → DeactivateAsync
API_ADMIN -> DB_USERS : AdminOwnersService.GetAsync: an owner? (404 owner_not_found,\nalso for a player or an admin), before the body [SELECT]
API_ADMIN -> API_ADMIN : Validates reason: required, trimmed, ≤ 500 (400)
API_ADMIN -> CC_AUTHZ : adminId = ICurrentUser.UserId (from the session, never from the request)
group Transaction (TryChangeAsync)
  API_ADMIN -> DB_USERS : UPDATE users SET deactivated_at = now WHERE id = … AND\ndeactivated_at IS NULL [ExecuteUpdate]
  alt 0 rows (already deactivated, or another admin won)
    API_ADMIN -> DB_USERS : ROLLBACK [SQL]
    API_ADMIN --> WEB_F_ADMIN : 422 owner_already_deactivated
  else 1 row
    API_ADMIN -> DB_STATUSCHG : OwnerStatusChange.Record(ownerId, Deactivated, reason, adminId,\nnow) [INSERT]
    API_ADMIN -> DB_REFRESH : Revokes all the owner's refresh tokens [UPDATE … SET revoked_at\nWHERE user_id = … AND revoked_at IS NULL]
    API_ADMIN -> DB_USERS : COMMIT [SQL]
    API_ADMIN -> DB_USERS : GetAsync again (futureBookings: bookings that stay\nconfirmed) [SELECT]
    API_ADMIN --> WEB_F_ADMIN : 200 AdminOwnerDetailResponse
    WEB_F_ADMIN -> WEB_F_ADMIN : invalidateQueries(['admin'])
  end
end
note over WEB_F_ADMIN, DB_REFRESH: No booking is cancelled. The access token already issued is valid for up to 15 min (accepted).\nAfterwards: login, refresh, public pages and new bookings refuse through the\ndeactivated_at checks.
@enduml
